          "type": "user",
          "text": "# Handoff summary: Python SDK AAC-only support\n\n---\n\n## 1. Goal\n\n- **Stop using declarative YAML** in the Python SDK.\n- **Use only AAC (Analytics as Code)** everywhere: load, store, deploy.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Context\n\n- **AAC format**: Human-oriented, snake_case, one object type per file; `analytics/` layout with `gooddata.yaml`; schemas in gdc-analytics-as-code `packages/code-schemas/schemas/v1/`.\n- **Declarative format**: API-oriented, camelCase, `gooddata_layouts/` with `organization_id/workspaces/workspace_id/analytics_model/` (metrics, visualization_objects, etc.).\n- **GoodData Cloud API** already has **AAC endpoints**; no backend changes are required.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Backend (GoodData Cloud) – already supports AAC\n\n- **Endpoints:**\n  - `GET/PUT /api/v1/aac/workspaces/{workspaceId}/analyticsModel`\n  - `GET/PUT /api/v1/aac/workspaces/{workspaceId}/logicalModel`\n- **gooddata-api-client** already exposes: `AACAnalyticsModelApi`, `AACLogicalDataModelApi` with `get_analytics_model_aac`, `set_analytics_model_aac`, `get_logical_model_aac`, `set_logical_model_aac`.\n- Official Cloud API docs include AAC schemas (e.g. `AacAnalyticsModel`, `AacLogicalModel`, `AacVisualization`, etc.).\n\n**Conclusion:** Backend consumes AAC directly; Python SDK only needs to send AAC (and optionally read/write AAC YAML).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Current Python SDK behavior (to replace)\n\n- **Deploy:** Uses `gd stream-out` (Node.js CLI from gdc-analytics-as-code) to turn AAC → declarative, then uses declarative layout API. Requires `gd` at `~/.gooddata/node_modules/.bin/gd`.\n- **Store/load:** Uses **declarative** layout under `gooddata_layouts/` (camelCase, `analytics_model/visualization_objects/`, etc.).\n- **Config:** Can use `gooddata.yaml` (AacConfig) for auth; deploy still goes through declarative + `gd stream-out`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Target behavior (AAC-only)\n\n- **Deploy:** Read AAC from disk (e.g. `analytics/` + `gooddata.yaml`), parse to API models, call:\n  - `set_logical_model_aac(workspace_id, aac_logical_model)`\n  - `set_analytics_model_aac(workspace_id, aac_analytics_model)`\n- **Store (backup):** Call `get_*_aac`, then write AAC YAML (snake_case, one file per object, `analytics/datasets/`, `analytics/metrics/`, `analytics/visualisations/`, etc.).\n- **Load:** Read AAC YAML from disk, parse to API models, then `set_*_aac` (or equivalent).\n- **No** dependency on `gd` CLI or declarative layout for these flows.\n- **No** use of `gooddata_layouts/` for the new AAC-only path.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Development / test setup (agreed)\n\n- **Local:** gooddata-python-sdk repo (implement + test).\n- **Backend:** GoodData Cloud (remote); no local backend or Docker required.\n- **Verification:** Cloud UI to confirm visualizations/dashboards after deploy.\n- **Reference only (no need to run):** gdc-analytics-as-code for AAC schemas, conversion logic, and example YAML (e.g. `packages/code-schemas/`, `packages/code/src/convertors/declarative/`, `packages/code/tests/examples/project6/`, `project7/`).\n\n---\n\n## 7. What the other agent should do in the Python SDK repo\n\n1. **AAC YAML ↔ API models**\n   - Parse AAC YAML (datasets, date datasets, metrics, visualisations, dashboards, plugins, attribute hierarchies) into the models used by the AAC API (e.g. `AacLogicalModel`, `AacAnalyticsModel` and their nested types).\n   - Serialize API responses back to AAC YAML (same layout and naming as gdc-analytics-as-code).\n\n2. **Replace declarative deploy with AAC deploy**\n   - For a given workspace and path (e.g. project root with `gooddata.yaml` and `analytics/`):\n     - Load LDM from `analytics/datasets/`, `analytics/dates/` (or equivalent) → build `AacLogicalModel` → `set_logical_model_aac`.\n     - Load analytics from `analytics/metrics/`, `analytics/visualisations/`, `analytics/dashboards/`, etc. → build `AacAnalyticsModel` → `set_analytics_model_aac`.\n   - Remove or bypass the `gd stream-out` + declarative put path for this flow.\n\n3. **Replace declarative store/load with AAC**\n   - **Store:** `get_*_aac` for the workspace, then write AAC YAML into `analytics/` (and optionally keep `gooddata.yaml`).\n   - **Load:** Read AAC YAML from `analytics/` (and `gooddata.yaml` if needed), build `AacLogicalModel` and `AacAnalyticsModel`, call `set_*_aac`.\n   - Stop using `gooddata_layouts/` for the primary path (or keep it only for backward compatibility behind a flag if required).\n\n4. **Config and profile**\n   - Keep using `gooddata.yaml` (AacConfig) for host/token/workspace when running in an AAC project; ensure deploy/load/store use the same path resolution.\n\n5. **Tests and compatibility**\n   - Add tests that deploy from AAC YAML to GoodData Cloud and (if possible) validate via API or exported state.\n   - Optionally keep a compatibility path for declarative layout (e.g. env flag or separate entrypoint) if the product still needs it; document that the default/canonical path is AAC-only.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Reference material (gdc-analytics-as-code, read-only)\n\n- **AAC layout:** `analytics/datasets/`, `analytics/dates/`, `analytics/metrics/`, `analytics/visualisations/`, `analytics/dashboards/`, etc.; `gooddata.yaml` at project root.\n- **Schemas:** `packages/code-schemas/schemas/v1/` (e.g. dataset, metric, visualisation, dashboard).\n- **Conversion (for reference):** `packages/code/src/convertors/declarative/toDeclarative.ts`, `fromDeclarative.ts` and `to/`, `from/` subdirs (AAC ↔ declarative).\n- **Example AAC YAML:** `packages/code/tests/examples/project6/`, `project7/` (e.g. `analytics/line_chart_1.yaml`, `column_chart_1.yaml`).\n\n---\n\n## 9. One-sentence summary\n\n**Switch gooddata-python-sdk to AAC-only: parse and emit AAC YAML and use the existing GoodData Cloud AAC API (`set_analytics_model_aac` / `set_logical_model_aac`, and get_*_aac for store); remove reliance on declarative layout and `gd stream-out` for the main deploy/load/store flow.**",
